1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.200
Ready to create your first Dynamic Data Export report?

2
00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:06.733
Let's walk through the process step-by-step.

3
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:11.033
First, click Dynamic Data Export in the left navigation pane.

4
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:13.266
If this is your first time,

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.200
you'll see a Create Report button in the top right corner.

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.400
Click this button to get started.

7
00:00:19.266 --> 00:00:24.266
you have existing reports, click Actions, and then click Create a Report.

8
00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:30.099
Give your report a clear title and description. This helps you find it later.

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.133
Then choose your chart type.

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.233
for detailed data,

11
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.133
line for trends over time,

12
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.166
or pie for proportions.

13
00:00:38.466 --> 00:00:41.299
We'll cover when to use each type in the next video.

14
00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.499
Next, set your date range.

15
00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:47.166
You can pick from preset options like

16
00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:48.899
this month or last quarter,

17
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.366
or select custom for specific dates.

18
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:57.321
For table and line charts, you can also choose how data is grouped,

19
00:00:57.321 --> 00:00:59.632
in daily or weekly intervals.

20
00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:05.933
Note that for custom ranges over 90 days, only weekly intervals are supported.

21
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.962
Now for the important part, selecting your measures. 

22
00:01:09.962 --> 00:01:14.736
Choose what data you want to analyze, like screen time or battery level, 

23
00:01:14.737 --> 00:01:18.266
then pick a calculation method, like average or sum,

24
00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:20.866
For table in line chart reports,

25
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.366
you can add up to 10 measures by clicking

26
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.800
Add measure.

27
00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:29.159
Dimensions come next. These depend on your measures.

28
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.421
For example, if you selected screen time

29
00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:35.714
you might choose Application name as your dimensions. 

30
00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:40.424
The system will show you which dimensions are compatible with your selected measures. 

31
00:01:40.424 --> 00:01:45.695
 If your selected dimension is not compatible, you'll see an error in the tool tip. 

32
00:01:45.696 --> 00:01:52.943
Just like with measures, you can add multiple dimensions to table and line chart reports by clicking add dimensions. 

33
00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:57.531
For our example, adding a second dimension like device model ,

34
00:01:57.531 --> 00:02:02.466
would allow us to compare the screen times of different device models running the same app.

35
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.184
If you selected a table report, you're almost done. 

36
00:02:07.184 --> 00:02:11.966
Simply click create and wait for your report to be generated.

37
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.616
For line and pie chart reports, you may be required to 

38
00:02:15.616 --> 00:02:18.832
select a filter, depending on the dimensions you selected.

39
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:24.286
If required, you'll see an error message letting you know which filter to use. 

40
00:02:24.287 --> 00:02:27.266
We'll cover how to use filters in another video.

41
00:02:27.266 --> 00:02:30.767
Back on the DDE page, you'll see an in-progress 

42
00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.405
status while your report is being generated.

43
00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:36.444
Once complete, you'll see a download link, 

44
00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:40.499
click it to download a copy for offline viewing or sharing

45
00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.399
Great job!

46
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.669
You've created your first report, but which chart type should you choose? 

47
00:02:47.669 --> 00:02:50.032
That's exactly what we'll cover next.

